      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GREEN WINTER (1) jumped straight to the front and defied all challengers to salute on debut over 1400m at Kembla last start. Big chance he will get an uncontested lead here so a repeat performance is certainly on the cards. Another last start maiden winner in FLYING ARABESQUE (2) looks a threat. Tried over the mile for the first time last Saturday at Kembla and closed a shade too well to get the cash at start four. Can kick on with the confidence growing at each appearance. RIBBLE LACE (3) led for the judge when resuming over 1300m at Hawkesbury recently and tried hard but found one better over the concluding stages. Fitter for that run and is far more at home out to today's journey. GEMTIKI (4) won a maiden two back over 1750m at Hawkesbury then struggled when extended to 2000m last time. Can do better back to this distance. Hard to see the others playing a role in the finish, with SONNIG (5) probably the pick of them.",
